	(text "Rev B: TRS MIDI Type A and Type B\nMIDI OUT (3.3V, CA-033): U3 buffers IO39/IO42 from +3.3V, so the output also works on battery.\n  Ring R4 = 33R (RA), tip R6 = 10R (RC). Loop resistance is 43R in either mode.\n  Type A: ring = IO42 held HIGH (source), tip = IO39 UART TX (sink).\n  Type B: tip = IO39 held HIGH (source), ring = IO42 UART TX (sink).\n  At reset IO39 has its internal pull-up and R7 pulls IO42 up: both outputs HIGH, no loop current.\nMIDI IN: D53-D56 Schottky bridge steers current through the 6N138 LED in either\n  polarity, so Type A and Type B senders both work with no setting. D52 removed (redundant).\nJ2/J3: board footprint is the through-hole SJ1-3515; MPN corrected from SJ2-3593A-SMT-TR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.15 124.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5f4f1657-1b4a-46ed-a8d3-d225efb2f86e")
	)
